Debian 13 update (2026-10-01)
----------------------------
See QUALIFICATION-DEBIAN13 for the native amd64/arm64 package qualification.
Ubuntu-only scope statements below describe the initial packaging checkpoint.

Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the process module
=============================================

The native module and qpp compiler metadata belong to qore-process-module.
HTML documentation and upstream test examples belong to the optional
qore-process-module-doc package. Debhelper creates matching debug symbols.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native build environment containing the packaged Qore runtime
and libqore-dev, then install the Build-Depends from debian/control. The current
qualification target is Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages.
Other distributions and architectures need their own qualified SDK, Boost 1.90
development packages and native build/test run. Cross builds are rejected
because qpp and Qore execute during compilation.

The build uses distribution compiler/hardening flags and system Boost headers
and Boost.Filesystem. It retains the patched Boost.Process 1.90.0 implementation
as a private static library inside the module. Upstream Boost 1.90.0 lacks the
Linux empty-command-line crash fix from commit 350c2a225 and the macOS argument
parsing fix from 2ab3b843a. Replacing this implementation with the unpatched
distribution library would lose those fixes. Review those patches when updating
Boost; the exact system Boost version check prevents mixing incompatible headers.
No separate Boost library is installed by this package.

The +ds original archive excludes unused bundled Boost components, tests and
documentation. The complete exclusion list is in debian/copyright. Retained
Boost.Process code carries the Boost Software License and its copyright notices.

Native Qore modules resolve Qore symbols at load time without linking libqore.
debian/rules derives a minimum runtime and libqore SONAME package dependency from
the installed SDK; dh_shlibdeps supplies other shared-library dependencies.
The runtime package is not Multi-Arch: same because it requires the native Qore
interpreter and includes shared compiler metadata. There are no AOT user modules
or Qore dependency trailers in this module; ordinary dh_strip is appropriate.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot version sorts before
the eventual 2.2.0 release. From a clean committed checkout, export the sources
without debian/, repack using debian/copyright's Files-Excluded list (for example
with mk-origtargz --repack --repack-suffix +ds), and name the original archive:

    qore-process-module_2.2.0~git20261004.1+ds.orig.tar.xz

Extract it into qore-process-module-2.2.0~git20261004.1+ds, copy debian/ there,
and create the source package with dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc. Extract the .dsc
with dpkg-source -x in a clean build directory. With dependencies preinstalled,
build as an unprivileged user with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

The repacked source requires USE_SYSTEM_BOOST_DEPENDENCIES=ON, which debian/rules
sets explicitly. The complete Git checkout retains the ordinary bundled build.
Architecture-only builds (-B) do not need Doxygen; architecture-independent
builds (-A) produce documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc suppress documentation; the profile also omits the doc
package. Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

The upstream process suite runs against the new module during the build,
including child input/output, exit status, signals, pipelines, sandbox and
process-information tests. Python and procps are test dependencies; no external
service is needed. Installed autopkgtests run the same suite away from the build
tree, then use the installed SDK and metadata to compile and run a program with
named Process::run arguments.

Check source/binary Lintian, detached debug symbols and hardening, installation
without libqore-dev, documentation/debug coinstallation, dpkg -V, purge/reinstall,
and reproducibility from two distinct build directories. Retain the exact source
commit, source/package hashes, dependency versions and logs. Publishing to the
testing PPA is separate from approval for a final general release.
